<protocol name="discovery_mindset" type="cross_cutting" agent="pm">

## PURPOSE

Intelligent routing through dependency analysis.
Load on: First message of any workflow.

---

## DEPENDENCY-BASED REASONING

**Don't follow prescribed chains. BUILD the dependency graph from user intent.**

### Step 1: Identify NEEDED Agents

| Question | Which Agents? |
|----------|---------------|
| Need to see what's IN image? | visual_analyst |
| Need external/market context? | product_analyst |
| Need to query OUR catalog? | catalog_analyst |
| Need visual output created? | creative_specialist |
| Need catalog records modified? | catalog_specialist |

**User intent determines which agents are NEEDED, not workflow templates.**

### Step 2: Map Dependencies

For each needed agent, ask: **"What does this agent REQUIRE to do its job?"**

| Agent | Hard Dependencies | Optional Context |
|-------|-------------------|------------------|
| visual_analyst | Image path | (none - always first for images) |
| product_analyst | Product name/description | visual_analysis.md (if from image) |
| catalog_analyst | Product name/family context | visual_analysis.md, product_research.md |
| creative_specialist | Image path, material context | visual_analysis.md, product_research.md |
| catalog_specialist | Product/family data | visual_analysis.md, product_research.md, asset_id |

**Hard dependency = MUST have. Optional = enriches output but not required.**

### Step 3: Build Execution Waves

**Waves execute sequentially. Within each wave, tasks run in parallel.**

```
Wave N: All agents whose dependencies are satisfied
  ↓ (WAIT for wave to complete)
Wave N+1: All agents whose dependencies are NOW satisfied
  ↓ (WAIT for wave to complete)
...continue until all needed agents executed
```

**The algorithm:**
```
NEEDED = [list of agents user needs]
DONE = []
WAVE = 1

while NEEDED not empty:
  READY = agents in NEEDED whose dependencies are in DONE
  if READY is empty: ERROR - circular dependency or missing prerequisite

  Execute all agents in READY in parallel
  DONE += READY
  NEEDED -= READY
  WAVE += 1
```

---

## [CRITICAL] IMAGE ANALYSIS BOUNDARY

**When image is involved, visual_analyst is ALMOST ALWAYS Wave 1.**

Why? Other agents need to know WHAT'S in the image before they can reason about it.

**Exception:** When you need to verify catalog context BEFORE looking at image.

| Scenario | Visual First? | Why |
|----------|---------------|-----|
| [image] + "add this" | ✅ YES | Need to see what it is |
| [image] + "update product X" | ❓ MAYBE | Might check catalog for X first, then visual |
| [image] + "is this ours?" | ❌ NO | Quick catalog check first, then visual if needed |
| [image] + "process this" | ✅ YES | Pure image work |
| [image] + "compare to existing" | ❓ MAYBE | Catalog first to know what to compare |

**Default: Visual first. Override only when catalog/product check is prerequisite to visual analysis.**

